selector_to_html = {"a[href=\"#distributed-bends-continuous\"]": "<h3 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Distributed bends: <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Continuous</span></code><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#distributed-bends-continuous\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h3><p>The rounded-bend correlations are well established, but they book the whole\nbend as one loss coefficient at one diameter, so they require the same bore at\nboth tangent stations. Say the bore also flares out along the pipe, here from\n25 mm to 90 mm. A <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">RoundedBend</span></code> cannot represent that, so we use a\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Continuous</span></code> bend instead:</p>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/ducts/pipe/Pipe.html#pyskyfire.ducts.pipe.Pipe.solve\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.pipe.Pipe.solve\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">solve</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">inlet_state</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/thermo/state/FluidState.html#pyskyfire.thermo.state.FluidState\" title=\"pyskyfire.thermo.state.FluidState\"><span class=\"pre\">FluidState</span></a></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">mass_flow</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">transport</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">inlet_swirl</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0.0</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">friction_model</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></a></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">'fluids'</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">bend_length_scale</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></a></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">'hydraulic'</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span> <span class=\"sig-return\"><span class=\"sig-return-icon\">\u2192</span> <span class=\"sig-return-typehint\"><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/ducts/pipe/DuctResult.html#pyskyfire.ducts.pipe.DuctResult\" title=\"pyskyfire.ducts.pipe.DuctResult\"><span class=\"pre\">DuctResult</span></a></span></span></dt><dd><p>March irreversible pressure losses from inlet to outlet.</p><p><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Straight</span></code> and <code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Continuous</span></code> connections charge wall\nfriction on the hydraulic diameter, the latter times the curvature\nmultiplier, along the helix a swirling flow follows, plus the loss of\nany change of area (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#pyskyfire.ducts.pipe.Pipe.area_change_loss_coefficient\" title=\"pyskyfire.ducts.pipe.Pipe.area_change_loss_coefficient\"><code class=\"xref py py-attr docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">area_change_loss_coefficient</span></code></a>). A\n<code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">RoundedBend</span></code> charges its complete loss coefficient. Every loss\nis on the through-flow head <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">rho*c_m**2/2</span></code>. Acceleration and heat\ntransfer are intentionally absent: a change of area alters the\nvelocities, and so the static pressure, but adds no reversible term\nto the marched stagnation pressure.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#give-a-pipe-swirl\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Give a pipe swirl<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#give-a-pipe-swirl\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>A pipe, with or without a core, can carry swirl about its centreline. Give the\ncircumferential velocity at the inlet\u2019s mean radius, <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">pipe.r_mean</span></code>, which is\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">(D</span> <span class=\"pre\">+</span> <span class=\"pre\">d)/4</span></code>, and a quarter of the bore without a core:</p>", "a[href=\"#lumped-bends-roundedbend\"]": "<h3 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Lumped bends: <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">RoundedBend</span></code><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#lumped-bends-roundedbend\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h3><p>Here is how to define the nodes and use the <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">bend</span></code> attribute:</p>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/thermo/fluid/Fluid.html#pyskyfire.thermo.fluid.Fluid\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.thermo.fluid.Fluid\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.thermo.fluid.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">Fluid</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">type</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">propellants</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">fractions</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">basis</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">'mass'</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">precision</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">3</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Mixture helper for fluids.</p><p>Stores a set of component names and composition.</p><p class=\"rubric\">Notes</p><p>Fractions are re-normalized internally when converting to mole basis to\nguard against small rounding errors.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#nodes-and-stations\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Nodes and stations<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#nodes-and-stations\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>There are two kinds of point in a pipe definition, and it is worth keeping them\napart:</p>", "a[href=\"#worked-example-rl10-tubing\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Worked example: RL10 tubing<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#worked-example-rl10-tubing\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">validation/RL10/plumbing/</span></code> builds real RL10 tubing from the fabrication\ndrawings, one module per component. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">bending_table.py</span></code> is the reusable part:\nit converts a tube-bending table \u2013 straight lengths, bend angles, bend radii,\nand the dihedral rotation between consecutive bend planes \u2013 into <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">PathNode</span></code>\ncontrol vertices, absorbing the tangent distance <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">R</span> <span class=\"pre\">*</span> <span class=\"pre\">tan(angle</span> <span class=\"pre\">/</span> <span class=\"pre\">2)</span></code> into\nboth legs at each corner and carrying bend planes by rolling the bend binormal\nabout the intervening straight. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">turbine_discharge_duct.py</span></code> is one such table,\nwith the bore taken from the drawing\u2019s OD and wall callouts.</p><p>Those pipes are built but not yet wired into the cycle in <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">sizer_sim.py</span></code>,\nwhich still represents each duct as a <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">SimpleDuctBlock</span></code> on a calibrated\npressure ratio. A ratio covers a whole network leg, so it can only be replaced\nonce every component along that leg exists.</p>", "a[href=\"#route-a-pipe-station-by-station\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Route a pipe station by station<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#route-a-pipe-station-by-station\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>The two routes above are conveniences. You can also skip them and supply the\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">PathStation</span></code>s and the connections between them yourself: the exact objects\nthe solver marches over. Here seven stations are placed by hand on a quarter\ncircle of 0.2 m radius, between a straight leg up and a straight leg across,\nand the arc\u2019s six intervals are joined by <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Continuous()</span></code> connections:</p>", "a[href=\"#define-and-solve-a-pipe\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Define and solve a pipe<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#define-and-solve-a-pipe\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p>A <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Pipe</span></code> in Pyskyfire is an object that transports fluid along a <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Path</span></code>. A path\nis a sequence of <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">PathStation</span></code> points joined by connections, and each\nconnection says how the pressure loss between its two stations is computed.\nThe program is set up this way so that a host of different 1D pipe models can\nbe used interchangeably along the same pipe.</p><p>All the code on this page comes from <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">examples/pipe/pipe_paths.py</span></code>, which also\nwrites every figure shown here.</p>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/viz/core/PlotBase.html#pyskyfire.viz.core.PlotBase.save_html\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.viz.core.PlotBase.save_html\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">save_html</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">path</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></a></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd></dd>", "a[href=\"3d-scenes.html\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Assemble a 3D scene<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#assemble-a-3d-scene\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Scene</span></code> combines component geometry and simulation fields in a common coordinate\nsystem. Use metres, radians, pascals, kelvin, and other base SI units. There are\nno unit-conversion arguments. Scene geometry illustrates the simulated model;\nCAD export remains a separate workflow.</p>", "a[href=\"#follow-the-pressure-along-a-flaring-pipe\"]": "<h3 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Follow the pressure along a flaring pipe<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#follow-the-pressure-along-a-flaring-pipe\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h3><p>The flared pipe is solved exactly like the others; its 67 stations are already\nin place. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">viz.PlotPipePressure</span></code> shows its static and stagnation pressure:</p>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/ducts/path/PathStation.html#pyskyfire.ducts.path.PathStation\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.path.PathStation\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.ducts.path.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">PathStation</span></span></dt><dd><p>A physical centerline station shared by flow components.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/viz/plot_ducts/PlotPipePressureLoss.html#pyskyfire.viz.plot_ducts.PlotPipePressureLoss\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.viz.plot_ducts.PlotPipePressureLoss\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.viz.plot_ducts.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">PlotPipePressureLoss</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></span><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">results</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">labels</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">markers</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">True</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">template</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">'plotly_white'</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Bases: <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/viz/core/PlotBase.html#pyskyfire.viz.core.PlotBase\" title=\"pyskyfire.viz.core.PlotBase\"><code class=\"xref py py-obj docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.viz.core.PlotBase</span></code></a></p><p>Cumulative irreversible pressure loss against arc length for solved pipes.</p><p>The loss at each station is the inlet stagnation pressure less the\nstagnation pressure there, so every curve starts at zero and ends at the\nresult\u2019s <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">total_pressure_loss</span></code>. Inputs are as for\n<code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">PlotPipePressure</span></code>.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/ducts/pipe/DuctResult.html#pyskyfire.ducts.pipe.DuctResult.total_pressure_loss\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.pipe.DuctResult.total_pressure_loss\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">property</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">total_pressure_loss</span></span><span class=\"property\"><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a></span></dt><dd><p>Total irreversible pressure loss [Pa].</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#put-a-pipe-in-an-engine-network\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Put a pipe in an engine network<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#put-a-pipe-in-an-engine-network\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">PipeBlock</span></code> returns the outlet network station, emits <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">dp_fuel_feed</span></code>, and stores\nthe detailed <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">DuctResult</span></code> in <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">network.block_results[\"fuel_feed\"]</span></code> after network\nconvergence. Valves and other discrete devices remain separate network blocks.</p>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/ducts/path/PathNode.html#pyskyfire.ducts.path.PathNode\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.path.PathNode\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.ducts.path.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">PathNode</span></span></dt><dd><p>Human-friendly route vertex consumed by <code class=\"xref py py-func docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">generate_path_stations()</span></code>.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#route-a-pipe-along-a-curve\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Route a pipe along a curve<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#route-a-pipe-along-a-curve\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Path.from_curve()</span></code> makes a path from a curve: a spline, a helix, or any shape\nyou can write as a function. Here a SciPy <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">CubicSpline</span></code> routes a pipe between\ntwo flanges, one at the origin facing up and one at <span class=\"math notranslate nohighlight\">\\((0.5, 0.4, 0.6)\\)</span> facing\nalong <span class=\"math notranslate nohighlight\">\\(+x\\)</span>, through one waypoint between them. Its end conditions fix the\ndirection at each end, so the pipe leaves and enters both flanges square to\nthem:</p>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/ducts/path/Path.html#pyskyfire.ducts.path.Path.from_nodes\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.path.Path.from_nodes\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">classmethod</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">from_nodes</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">nodes</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd></dd>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/viz/scene/Scene.html#pyskyfire.viz.scene.Scene.add\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.viz.scene.Scene.add\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">add</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">component</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">name</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">transform</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">position</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">rotation</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">parent</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">anchor</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">attach_to</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">tags</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">()</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd></dd>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/thermo/state/FluidStateResolver.html#pyskyfire.thermo.state.FluidStateResolver\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.thermo.state.FluidStateResolver\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.thermo.state.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">FluidStateResolver</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">transport</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">p_ref</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Resolve fluid states from <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">(h,</span> <span class=\"pre\">p)</span></code>, with cached saturation data.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/viz/plot_ducts/PlotPipePressure.html#pyskyfire.viz.plot_ducts.PlotPipePressure\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.viz.plot_ducts.PlotPipePressure\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.viz.plot_ducts.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">PlotPipePressure</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></span><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">results</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">labels</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">static</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">True</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">stagnation</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">True</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">markers</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">True</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">template</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">'plotly_white'</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Bases: <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/viz/core/PlotBase.html#pyskyfire.viz.core.PlotBase\" title=\"pyskyfire.viz.core.PlotBase\"><code class=\"xref py py-obj docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.viz.core.PlotBase</span></code></a></p><p>Static and/or stagnation pressure against arc length for solved pipes.</p><p>Each input is a <code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">DuctResult</span></code>, or any result with\nthe same <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">s</span></code>, <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">p_stagnation</span></code> and <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">p_static</span></code> station arrays. Markers\nsit on the <code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">PathStation</span></code> positions the solver\nevaluated; between them the line is only a straight join, so a lumped\n<code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">RoundedBend</span></code> shows as one step across its arc.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#draw-a-pipe-in-a-3d-scene\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Draw a pipe in a 3D scene<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#draw-a-pipe-in-a-3d-scene\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">PipeComponent</span></code> reads the pipe\u2019s own geometry and reopens lumped <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">RoundedBend</span></code>\nconnections into arcs for drawing only. Passing the <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">DuctResult</span></code> colours the\ntube by any solved quantity, here the static pressure. A pipe with a core is\ndrawn as the core inside a translucent bore, the core only where it runs. See\n<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"3d-scenes.html\"><span class=\"std std-doc\">Assemble a 3D scene</span></a> for placement against a chamber or a pump.</p>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/thermo/state/FluidStateResolver.html#pyskyfire.thermo.state.FluidStateResolver.from_tp\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.thermo.state.FluidStateResolver.from_tp\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">from_tp</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">T</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">p</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span> <span class=\"sig-return\"><span class=\"sig-return-icon\">\u2192</span> <span class=\"sig-return-typehint\"><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/thermo/state/FluidState.html#pyskyfire.thermo.state.FluidState\" title=\"pyskyfire.thermo.state.FluidState\"><span class=\"pre\">FluidState</span></a></span></span></dt><dd><p>Resolve the bulk state from <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">(T,</span> <span class=\"pre\">p)</span></code>, for the temperature march.</p><p>Cannot represent a two-phase state \u2013 that is the whole limitation of\nthe temperature march \u2013 so the phase is reported as\n<code class=\"xref py py-data docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">PHASE_UNKNOWN</span></code> unless the fluid is known to be supercritical.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/ducts/path/Straight.html#pyskyfire.ducts.path.Straight\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.path.Straight\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.ducts.path.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">Straight</span></span></dt><dd><p>Distributed straight-pipe friction between two adjacent stations.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/ducts/pipe/Pipe.html#pyskyfire.ducts.pipe.Pipe\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.pipe.Pipe\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.ducts.pipe.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">Pipe</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">path</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">connections</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">diameter</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">core_diameter</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0.0</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">roughness</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">|</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">Callable</span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">[</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">[</span></span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">]</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">,</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">]</span></span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0.0</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">max_diameter_change</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0.02</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>A circular duct swept along a path, with an optional core, and its loss solver.</p><p>The section normal to the path is a circular bore of <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">diameter</span></code>, with a\nconcentric core of <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">core_diameter</span></code> inside it where that is not zero. A\nplain pipe has no core. A core may run the whole length, as in coaxial\nlines, or only part of it: it may start from a point, as a turbine\u2019s nose\ndoes, and end, bluntly or tapering.</p><p>The march evaluates each connection at one section, the mean of its two\nends. Where the section varies, the pipe therefore splits\n<code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Straight</span></code> and <code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Continuous</span></code> connections itself until its\narea and hydraulic diameter each change by at most\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">max_diameter_change</span></code> (relative, the area as the diameter of the circle\nof the same area) across each piece, placing the extra stations where the\nsection changes fastest. A constant section is left exactly as supplied,\nand so is every <code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">RoundedBend</span></code>. <code class=\"xref py py-attr docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">path</span></code>, <code class=\"xref py py-attr docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">stations</span></code> and\nevery result refer to the resolved stations, which include all of the\nsupplied ones.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/ducts/pipe/DuctResult.html#pyskyfire.ducts.pipe.DuctResult.swirl_angle\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.pipe.DuctResult.swirl_angle\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">property</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">swirl_angle</span></span><span class=\"property\"><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://numpy.org/doc/stable/reference/generated/numpy.ndarray.html#numpy.ndarray\" title=\"(in NumPy v2.5)\"><span class=\"pre\">ndarray</span></a></span></dt><dd><p>Flow angle from the through-flow direction, <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">atan(c_u/c_m)</span></code> [rad].</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#give-a-pipe-a-core\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Give a pipe a core<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#give-a-pipe-a-core\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>A <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Pipe</span></code> can carry a concentric core inside its bore: a centrebody, a turbine\u2019s\nnose, or the inner line of coaxial tubing. Give its diameter as\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">core_diameter</span></code>, the same ways as <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">diameter</span></code>: a constant, one value per\nstation, or a function of arc length. Zero, the default, is no core.</p>", "a[href=\"#route-a-pipe-through-corners\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Route a pipe through corners<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#route-a-pipe-through-corners\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Path.from_nodes()</span></code> turns a list of <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">PathNode</span></code>s into stations and connections\nwith <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">generate_path_stations()</span></code>. Each corner is rounded by the bend its node\ncarries, and the bend can book its loss in one of two ways: as one lumped loss\nfor the whole bend, or as wall friction distributed along its arc.</p>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/thermo/state/FluidState.html#pyskyfire.thermo.state.FluidState\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.thermo.state.FluidState\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.thermo.state.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">FluidState</span></span></dt><dd><p>Resolved bulk fluid state at one axial station.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/thermo/transport/FluidTransport.html#pyskyfire.thermo.transport.FluidTransport\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.thermo.transport.FluidTransport\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.thermo.transport.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">FluidTransport</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">fluid</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/thermo/fluid/Fluid.html#pyskyfire.thermo.fluid.Fluid\" title=\"pyskyfire.thermo.fluid.Fluid\"><span class=\"pre\">Fluid</span></a></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>CoolProp-backed transport/thermo properties for a single fluid.</p><p>Thin wrapper around <strong>CoolProp</strong> that exposes convenient getters using a\n<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/thermo/fluid/Fluid.html#pyskyfire.thermo.fluid.Fluid\" title=\"pyskyfire.thermo.fluid.Fluid\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Fluid</span></code></a> to obtain the CoolProp fluid string.</p><p class=\"rubric\">Notes</p></dd>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/viz/components/PipeComponent.html#pyskyfire.viz.components.PipeComponent\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.viz.components.PipeComponent\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.viz.components.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">PipeComponent</span></span></dt><dd><p>Display an explicitly defined pipe; never route or modify a solver model.</p><p>The pipe supplies its own geometry. A <code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Pipe</span></code> offers\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">display_path(segments=...)</span></code>, which opens its rounded and continuous bend\nconnections into arcs for drawing without touching the solved model;\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">segments</span></code> sets the drawn sides per quarter turn. Any other object is read through <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">centerline</span></code>, an (N,3)\nCartesian polyline in metres, and <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">radius</span></code>, a positive scalar or one\nradius per station, and is drawn exactly as supplied. The local frame is\nthe frame of those coordinates (no implicit recentering).</p><p>A pipe with a core is drawn as a <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">\"core\"</span></code> surface, one per stretch the\ncore runs along, inside a translucent <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">\"bore\"</span></code> of <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">opacity</span></code>, both\nchildren of the returned node, which carries the bore\u2019s end anchors.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">results</span></code> is a <code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">DuctResult</span></code>, or a mapping of\nfield names to FieldData: point-associated with one value per station, or\ncell-associated with one value per connection. Station values are\ninterpolated along refined bends and repeated around each ring; connection\nvalues fill the rings spanning that connection. Every surface carries the\nsame fields.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/ducts/pipe/DuctResult.html#pyskyfire.ducts.pipe.DuctResult\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.pipe.DuctResult\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.ducts.pipe.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">DuctResult</span></span></dt><dd><p>Station states and per-interval diagnostics from a duct loss march.</p><p><code class=\"xref py py-meth docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Pipe.solve()</span></code> and <code class=\"xref py py-meth docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">solve()</span></code> both\nreturn one. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">p_stagnation</span></code> is the marched pressure: the inlet pressure\nless the irreversible losses up to each station. It includes the swirl\u2019s\ndynamic head. The march is adiabatic, so <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">T_stagnation</span></code> is the inlet\ntemperature at every station, and <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">states</span></code> and <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">density</span></code> are evaluated\nat the two.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">meridional_velocity</span></code> is the through-flow velocity <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">c_m</span></code> normal to the\nflow area, <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">swirl_velocity</span></code> the circumferential <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">c_u</span></code> at the mean\nradius, and <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">velocity</span></code> their magnitude, which without swirl is the\nthrough-flow velocity. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">T_static</span></code> is the stagnation temperature less\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">velocity**2/(2*cp)</span></code>, with <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">cp</span></code> taken at the same state as the\ndensity. Like <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">p_static</span></code> it is a first-order correction, not a\nstatic-state solution.</p><p>Per-interval arrays have one value fewer than the stations.\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">loss_coefficient</span></code> is referred to the through-flow head\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">rho*c_m**2/2</span></code> on the interval\u2019s mean section. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">darcy_factor</span></code> is the\nfactor applied, including any curvature multiplier, and NaN over a lumped\nbend.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">stations</span></code> and <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">connections</span></code> are a <code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Pipe</span></code>\u2019s resolved path, and\nNone for an <code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">AnnularDuct</span></code>. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">fluid</span></code> is the\nCoolProp name the transport carried, or None when it named none.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#compare-a-lumped-and-a-distributed-bend\"]": "<h3 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Compare a lumped and a distributed bend<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#compare-a-lumped-and-a-distributed-bend\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h3><p>To see how the two bend models differ, build the same corner again, with the\nsame constant 25 mm bore, but as a <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Continuous</span></code> bend, and solve it with the\nsame inlet and flow:</p>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/ducts/path/RoundedBend.html#pyskyfire.ducts.path.RoundedBend\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.path.RoundedBend\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.ducts.path.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">RoundedBend</span></span></dt><dd><p>A complete lumped rounded-bend loss between adjacent stations.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/ducts/path/Path.html#pyskyfire.ducts.path.Path.from_curve\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.path.Path.from_curve\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">classmethod</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">from_curve</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">curve</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">t_span</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">max_turn</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">math.radians(5.0)</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Sample a curve-like object into stations, as finely as its bends need.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">curve</span></code> is anything that maps a parameter <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">t</span></code> to a point: called\nwith an array of parameters it returns points of shape <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">(len(t),</span> <span class=\"pre\">3)</span></code>,\nor it returns one point per scalar <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">t</span></code>. SciPy\u2019s <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">CubicSpline</span></code>,\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">make_interp_spline</span></code> and <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">PchipInterpolator</span></code> qualify as they are, and\nso does a plain function. Planar points <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">(len(t),</span> <span class=\"pre\">2)</span></code> lie in the x-y\nplane. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">t_span</span></code> is the <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">(start,</span> <span class=\"pre\">end)</span></code> parameter range to follow.</p><p>Sampling is adaptive. Any interval whose curve turns by more than\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">max_turn</span></code> [rad] is halved, so stations crowd into tight bends and\nstay sparse along straight stretches. Each interval then becomes the\ncircular arc through its two stations and the curve\u2019s own midpoint: a\n<code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Continuous</span></code> carrying that arc\u2019s radius, length, center, and\nnormal, or a <code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Straight</span></code> where the three are collinear.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#solve-a-pipe\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Solve a pipe<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#solve-a-pipe\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>Here the rounded-bend pipe carries 2 kg/s of water, which is 4.1 m/s in the\n25 mm bore and a Reynolds number of about <span class=\"math notranslate nohighlight\">\\(1.2 \\times 10^5\\)</span>:</p>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/viz/scene/Scene.html#pyskyfire.viz.scene.Scene\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.viz.scene.Scene\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.viz.scene.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">Scene</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">title</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">'Pyskyfire</span> <span class=\"pre\">3D'</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">color_by</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">clim</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">show_axes</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">False</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Assemble components for desktop or standalone HTML display.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">anchor</span></code> names the added component\u2019s local anchor; <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">attach_to</span></code> is a\nworld-space Anchor. Attachment mates their outward x axes in opposition.\nIt is a one-time placement calculation, with no fluid-network constraints.\nExplicit placement and anchor placement are mutually exclusive.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">tags</span></code> labels the added node, a string or an iterable of them. Nodes\nsharing a tag appear together as one group in the HTML viewer, so a\ngrouping written into the script survives regenerating the results.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">show_axes</span></code> adds a corner orientation triad marking the scene axes\n(x red, y green, z blue). It is an orientation cue only, not a measuring\ngrid: it carries no ticks and does not indicate the origin or scale.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/network/blocks/PipeBlock.html#pyskyfire.network.blocks.PipeBlock\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.network.blocks.PipeBlock\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.network.blocks.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">PipeBlock</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">name</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></a></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">st_in</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></a></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">st_out</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></a></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">pipe</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/ducts/pipe/Pipe.html#pyskyfire.ducts.pipe.Pipe\" title=\"pyskyfire.ducts.pipe.Pipe\"><span class=\"pre\">Pipe</span></a></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">transport</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">friction_model</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></a></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">'fluids'</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">inlet_swirl</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0.0</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Bases: <code class=\"xref py py-obj docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">FluidBlock</span></code></p><p>Engine-network adapter for one explicitly resolved <code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Pipe</span></code>.</p><p>The contained pipe remains independently usable through <code class=\"xref py py-meth docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Pipe.solve()</span></code>.\nThis block only translates network stations into that public solver API and\nemits the resulting outlet station and <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">dp_&lt;name&gt;</span></code> loss signal.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/ducts/path/Path.html#pyskyfire.ducts.path.Path\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.path.Path\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.ducts.path.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">Path</span></span></dt><dd><p>Resolved stations and connections in order from inlet to outlet.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">s</span></code> is true arc length [m]. Geometry carries no bore diameter or state.\nUse <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#pyskyfire.ducts.path.Path.refined\" title=\"pyskyfire.ducts.path.Path.refined\"><code class=\"xref py py-meth docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">refined()</span></code></a> to choose the thermal/flow integration resolution.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#losses-where-the-area-changes\"]": "<h3 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Losses where the area changes<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#losses-where-the-area-changes\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h3><p>Where the flow area changes, the flow loses not only to wall friction but also\nto the change. Where the area grows, it loses to its own slowing, as a diffuser\ndoes; above about a 7\u00b0 full cone angle that loss exceeds the friction. Where\nthe area shrinks, it loses to its speeding up, as a contraction does: little\nfor a gentle taper, but about half the downstream velocity head at a sharp\nstep. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">solve</span></code> adds both on top of the friction, and\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">pipe.area_change_loss_coefficient</span></code> holds them for every connection.</p><p>A stretch over which the area keeps growing is treated as one diffuser, and\none over which it keeps shrinking as one contraction. Each ends where the area\nchanges the other way, or at a constant-section stretch longer than four\nhydraulic diameters, since the flow recovers there; a shorter one, such as a\nbend between two cones, leaves it one diffuser. A diffuser loses the expansion\nterm of Rennels\u2019 conical-diffuser correlation\n(<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">fluids.fittings.diffuser_conical</span></code>) for its two end diameters, and a\ncontraction the convergence term of his conical-contraction correlation\n(<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">contraction_conical</span></code>). Each is taken at the cone angle averaged with weight\nwhere the flow slows or speeds up. For a true cone that is Rennels\u2019 value, and\nfor a step his sudden-expansion or sharp-contraction loss. It does not depend\non how finely the pipe is split, and a nearly parallel stretch at either end\nof a steep cone does not water it down. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">pipe.cone_angle</span></code> gives the local full\ncone angle of every connection.</p>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/viz/scene/Scene.html#pyskyfire.viz.scene.Scene.save_html\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.viz.scene.Scene.save_html\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">save_html</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">path</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd></dd>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/ducts/path/Continuous.html#pyskyfire.ducts.path.Continuous\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.path.Continuous\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.ducts.path.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">Continuous</span></span></dt><dd><p>A locally resolved continuous-curvature connection.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">radius</span></code> is the exact centerline radius when known. If omitted on a\nmanually supplied layout, <code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Path</span></code> estimates it transparently from\nneighboring station triples using Menger curvature. Attached to a\n<code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">PathNode</span></code>, it rounds that corner with a circular arc of <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">radius</span></code>,\nwhich the generator emits as one connection carrying its exact arc\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">length</span></code>, <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">center</span></code> and <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">normal</span></code>. A constant-section arc needs no\nfurther stations; <code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Pipe</span></code> adds them where its section varies.</p></dd>"}
skip_classes = ["headerlink", "sd-stretched-link"]

window.onload = function () {
    for (const [select, tip_html] of Object.entries(selector_to_html)) {
        const links = document.querySelectorAll(` ${select}`);
        for (const link of links) {
            if (skip_classes.some(c => link.classList.contains(c))) {
                continue;
            }

            tippy(link, {
                content: tip_html,
                allowHTML: true,
                arrow: true,
                placement: 'auto-start', maxWidth: 600, interactive: false,
                onShow(instance) {MathJax.typesetPromise([instance.popper]).then(() => {});},
            });
        };
    };
    console.log("tippy tips loaded!");
};
